# EKATMA Department Portal — Next.js + PWA Migration Source of Truth

> **Purpose:** This file is the execution guide for Antigravity (and human developers) to convert the supplied **Bianca Dept** Figma Make codebase from React + Vite into a production-structured **Next.js App Router** application and make it an **installable PWA**, without losing, simplifying, redesigning, or inventing department-side functionality.
>
> **Source project inspected:** `Bianca Dept.zip`
>
> **Migration principle:** Preserve first. Refactor second. Integrate backend third. Do not redesign during migration.
>
> **Current recommended Next.js baseline at the time this guide was created and re-verified (23 Sep 2026):** Next.js **16.3.6 Active LTS** or a newer patched Active LTS available at execution time. Do not intentionally downgrade to an older vulnerable release.
>
> **Proofread status:** Re-checked against the supplied source tree, the EKATMA shared architecture requirements supplied with this project, and current official Next.js/Tailwind guidance. This revision additionally locks canonical domain contracts before M06+, scopes the Department PWA to `/department/`, adds explicit RAG/rule/dependency boundaries, fixes the test stack, prohibits static export, preserves Figma reference material, and adds a post-parity Department Pack abstraction so MIDC remains the first implementation rather than becoming the architecture.

