# 15. SIMPLE SERVICE WORKER BASELINE

A minimal worker may:

1. cache a named static shell set
2. serve an offline fallback for navigation failures
3. avoid intercepting sensitive API/auth calls
4. clean old cache versions on activate

Conceptual example only; adapt paths to the final build:

```js
const CACHE_PREFIX = 'ekatma-department-static-'
const STATIC_CACHE = `${CACHE_PREFIX}v1`
const OFFLINE_URL = '/department/offline.html'

self.addEventListener('install', (event) => {
  event.waitUntil(
    caches.open(STATIC_CACHE).then((cache) =>
      cache.addAll([
        OFFLINE_URL,
        '/assets/ekatma-logo.png',
        '/department/icons/pwa-192x192.png',
        '/department/icons/pwa-512x512.png',
      ])
    )
  )

  // Do not force skipWaiting() here by default. A newly installed worker must not
  // unexpectedly replace/reload an officer's page while unsaved form work exists.
})

self.addEventListener('activate', (event) => {
  event.waitUntil(
    Promise.all([
      caches.keys().then((keys) =>
        Promise.all(
          keys
            .filter((key) => key.startsWith(CACHE_PREFIX) && key !== STATIC_CACHE)
            .map((key) => caches.delete(key))
        )
      ),
      self.clients.claim(),
    ])
  )
})

self.addEventListener('fetch', (event) => {
  const request = event.request
  const url = new URL(request.url)

  if (request.method !== 'GET') return
  if (url.origin !== self.location.origin) return

  // Never SW-cache authenticated API/auth traffic by default.
  if (url.pathname.startsWith('/api/')) return
  if (url.pathname.startsWith('/auth/')) return

  // Navigations remain network-first. If the network is unavailable, return only
  // the static non-sensitive fallback, not a previously cached officer page.
  if (request.mode === 'navigate') {
    event.respondWith(
      fetch(request).catch(async () =>
        (await caches.match(OFFLINE_URL)) || Response.error()
      )
    )
  }
})
```

This example is intentionally conservative.

A richer offline strategy must be separately threat-modeled and reviewed.

