# 22A. CANONICAL DOMAIN CONTRACT RULES

Phase 3.5 creates the canonical domain contract; every later feature must reuse it.

## Identity rule

Never represent the same identity under different ad-hoc names/types across screens. For example, one Application ID must remain the same record through:

```text
Queue -> Overview -> Scrutiny -> Query -> Inspection -> Decision -> Dependency -> Compliance -> Audit
```

Use branded/opaque ID types to reduce accidental mixing of identifiers.

## State rule

Do not use a universal `status: string` model. Each state family has different semantics and must be typed separately.

UI badge labels/colors belong in a presentation mapping. Canonical state is not inferred from badge text.

## Entrepreneur/Department consistency rule

The Department frontend is not allowed to create a second interpretation of application/query/inspection/decision/dependency records. The intended architecture is:

```text
                 EKATMA SHARED BACKEND / DOMAIN

Business / Project / Business DNA / Dossier
                 │
        Regulatory Rule Engine
                 │
           Dependency Engine
                 │
Applications / Documents / Queries / Inspections
 Decisions / SLA / Compliance / Audit
                 │
       Canonical Shared API Contracts
              ┌──┴──┐
              │     │
      ENTREPRENEUR  DEPARTMENT
          APP          APP
```

The two frontends may present different views/actions, but a shared record must keep the same canonical identity/state/version semantics.

---

# 22B. REGULATORY RULE / RAG / DEPENDENCY BOUNDARIES

Keep these as explicit integrations rather than one generic `regulatory` blob.

Recommended feature boundaries:

```text
src/features/regulatory/rules/
src/features/regulatory/rag/
src/features/dependencies/
```

Conceptual responsibilities:

### Regulatory Rule Engine

- authoritative applicability/rule evaluation result
- versioned rule references
- structured conditions/results consumed by UI

### Dependency Engine

- authoritative dependency graph/state
- prerequisites
- locked/unlocked/blocking relationships
- next eligible workflow nodes

### RAG / Knowledge Service

- retrieves GRs/clauses/reference material
- explains rules in officer-friendly language
- supports bilingual assistance
- helps interpret regulatory changes
- returns citations/provenance where supported

### RAG must NOT own

- canonical application state
- canonical dependency state
- regulatory applicability decision
- payment state
- department approval/rejection
- workflow unlocking
- mutation of official records

The frontend consumes versioned authoritative rule/dependency results from backend services. RAG content is explanatory/retrieval assistance and must not silently mutate authoritative workflow state.

