Do not accept “same functionality” if visual hierarchy changed unintentionally.

## PWA tests

Verify:

- `/department/manifest.webmanifest` or the generated nested manifest resolves correctly
- Department icons resolve and maskable safe zone is correct
- installed app launches to `/department`
- unauthenticated navigation reaches `/department/login`
- exactly one Department worker controls only `/department/`
- Entrepreneur/root routes are not controlled by the Department worker if they coexist on the same origin
- worker update does not reload over unsaved form work
- old Department static caches are removed
- `/department/offline.html` renders with network disabled
- sensitive API/auth/page responses are not served from unsafe worker caches
- non-GET official mutations are not cached/replayed by default
- logout/session expiry behaves correctly in installed mode
- iOS Safari home-screen behavior is manually checked where in scope

For secure-context local testing, use an HTTPS-capable local setup such as current Next.js `next dev --experimental-https` when appropriate.

